From da9b94562bdcccde221ca876ed8a4232bac50818 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:04:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): keep claim publication reads off owner loop
 [daveey]

Initial FIFO reads were offloaded, but tracked postclaim publication reread admissions twice synchronously. The fixture often cancelled its ticker before observing that final stall. Stamp execution immediately on-loop, prepare storage off-loop without holding the stream lock, and fence publication against stream/overlay changes. Preserve synchronous callers and frozen source controls.

Causal handshake kills initial and postclaim offload mutants. Stale fence mutant fails 16 interleavings. Expanded focused tests pass; broader consumers and required CI remain gates.
